+/* ============================================================================
+ * TEMPORARY BENCH TEST -- SYNTHETIC RPM RAMP
+ * ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ * Why: the frame-rate fix on the RPM page can only be measured when RPM values
+ * actually arrive. Over BLE/ELM327 they arrive at ~10 Hz; with no Vgate/OBD
+ * adapter connected they arrive at 0 Hz, so `AtzPerf: ui_updates/s` stays 0.0
+ * and the interpolation cannot be observed on the bench.
+ *
+ * What: feeds obd_data's RPM/speed snapshot with a triangular ramp at a
+ * realistic ~10 Hz rate (deliberately NOT faster -- the point is to prove the
+ * page's own interpolation lifts the on-screen updates from ~10/s to ~60/s).
+ * The ramp must be injected at the snapshot source, not into `usRpm` further
+ * down, because the real-read block overwrites `usRpm` from the snapshot on
+ * every non-sweep tick.
